I don't really remember very much from the beginning of the game,
except that around dungeon level 3 some monster dropped crystal plate
mail, which is probably what kept me alive through the first part of
the game.  On level 4, I found the first co-aligned altar (out of 3).
I sacrificed until I got Magicbane, then set up my stash.  The stairs
to the mines were on the same level, but I skipped them and headed down
to do Sokoban.  On level 6, I found the only shop in the main dungeon
(it was used armor), but it didn't have anything good, so I kept going.
Sokoban had a bag of holding, which I like a lot better than
reflection in the early game.  Also, the bag was nice because my
crystal plate used up over half of my carrying capacity.  I think my
pet died somewhere right after Sokoban, but I don't really remember.

After Sokoban, I headed back up to do the mines.  Minetown's altar was
cross-aligned, unfortunately.  However, there were about 5 shops there,
including the general store I used for price-ID'ing things before I got
+oIdentify.  At the bottom of the mines, my telepathy picked up a mind
flayer, so I collected what I could (including a luckstone some monster
dropped) and left right away.

I don't remember much between finding the mind flayer and returning to
kill it, but I must have been to the Big Room and Rogue levels (Rogue
had the quest portal), because I know the mind flayer ate the knowledge
of those levels, along with all the other levels except for about three
of them.  It also got the appearances of almost every object I'd found
and 8 points of int (restored with a unicorn horn) before I ran away.
Fortunately, I remembered seeing a spellbook I didn't need, which I
blanked so I could write a +oIdentify (I think the marker was from my
starting inventory).

I ran around killing stuff until I was XL 14, then did the quest.  The
Dark One was a wimp; he only took a few hits to kill.  I got the Eye
(very nice artifact), the bell, and Frost Brand (just sitting on the
floor in the Dark One's dungeon), then headed back to go find Medusa.

Along the way, I found the second co-aligned altar on level 16 and
moved my stash of items down from level 4.  Then I kept going until I
ran into Medusa's island.  The stupid RNG put a peaceful gremlin on
that level, which (along with its 50 or so copies) drove me crazy every
time I tried to go past.  Finally I got to Medusa, who I killed with a
mirror, then smashed with force bolt (just in case).

After Medusa, I found the third and last altar in the dungeon.  When I
moved my stash down from level 16, I decided to leave the crystal plate
because I was too lazy to make two trips.  After that, I kept going
down until I found the castle on level 29.

The castle was pretty easy to clean out, except for the lich or two
that showed up.  After it was empty, I grabbed the wand and started
sorting all the armor the monsters had left into four piles for
polypiling: weapons, armor, tools, and gems.  Before I started
polypiling, I decided to drag my stash down to the castle, get
protection from the minetown priest, and check the armor shop to make
sure it didn't have anything I could use.

The first two parts of my plan worked pretty well.  I invoked the Eye,
which took me to Mine's End.  I killed the mind flayer there and
collected all the gems that were left.  Then I headed up and bought a
few points of protection, then to the armor store.  The store didn't
have anything useful.  I was already permanently invisible by then and
didn't have a mummy wrapping, so I teleported in and used the Eye to
leave.  Unfortunately, I chose to invoke the Eye while I was next to
the shopkeeper, so when I showed up in the Valley, there was an angry
shopkeeper next to me.  I killed him, but I didn't realize he was the
guy from the armor shop until I went back and found the Kops
everywhere.

Anyway, I took all my stuff for polypiling up to the castle and started
zapping the stacks with my wand of polymorph.  I got a few golems and a
lot of useful stuff, including most of the gems I ascended with, 2
magic markers, and 4 "oLS (but not until later, when I actually thought
of polypiling amulets & rings).  Eventually, I headed into Gehennom.

Gehennom wasn't very difficult, except for the fire traps scorching all
my good armor.  Juiblex was in the mines (summoned by my sacrifice of
an Elf), Baalzebub was bribed for a very low price (all but $200 was in
my BoH), and I smacked Asmodeus with a cockatrice corpse.  Orcus was
pretty easy too.  Vlad was even wimpier than the quest nemesis, and I
got my first "oLS from his tower.  I kept going until I found the fake
wizard tower with the portal and cleaned out the real tower (except for
killing the Wizard).  The second fake tower had another "oLS (I think I
already had some extras from my polypiling).  Finally, I got to the
bottom and marked the Vibrating Square.

Since I had brought my pick-axe (and lots of food), I started clearing
out wide passages (3-4 squares wide) between the stairs all the way up
to the top of the dungeon.  Then I headed back down to the castle to
finish making my ascension kit.  I had to wish for SDSM (I had
basically every other color of scales) and helm of brilliance
(accidentally vaporized it).  I also wished for a magic marker to write
finger of death (I already had Stormbringer when crowned, so I didn't
get anything).  Once I finished with all my armor, I started enchanting
my weapons... and accidentally vaporized Stormbringer (oops!).  Once I
had that, I collected all my gems and left them in a BoH on the stairs
on level 1.  I also had some water to bless, so I did a water prayer on
level 4.  The water prayer got me some extra holy water and a spellbook
of magic mapping.

I hadn't had any way to detect vaults before, so I headed to the castle
on foot, magic mapping every level from 11 to Medusa, looking for the
portal to Ludios.  I found it around level 19 and went through.

Clearing Ludios was lots of fun.  There was a chickatrice in the zoo,
which I killed quickly and used to make some statues.  Then I opened
the door and stood in the doorway waiting for anything brave enough to
come close.  By the time I was done, there were 3 huge piles of statues
right outside the door, and I had my second wand of death.  I decided
that I didn't need any more gold and I didn't know what I would wish
for if I got one from the throne, so I just took the Eye back to the
castle.

I made one final check to make sure I had everything, then invoked the
Eye again to get to Vlad's tower.  I headed down to the wizard's tower
and killed him with finger of death.  I then headed down to the
Vibrating Square with the Book.  Moloch's Sanctum was pretty easy,
since I had genocided liches and I could just zap the priests with
finger of death.  I also had the spell "detect unseen" which I used to
find the door to the inner room.  I fried the high priest with my new
favorite spell and grabbed the amulet.  I tried to get out of there
without using one of my cursed gain level potions, but something
summoned monsters all around me, so I ended up using one anyway.

Heading up to the castle was pretty easy because the mysterious force
left me alone most of the time, except for one time (on a pair of
no-teleport levels, of course).  I went past Juiblex's swamp and
Baalzebub's lair three or four times.  One of the times past
Baalzebub's lair, Yeenoghu appeared from somewhere and started
attacking me all the way through the next two levels.  I finally
managed to kill him a few levels before the castle.  The stupid Wizard
only showed up twice, and never had a chance to do anything but talk
before he got the finger of death again.  Finally I made it all the way
up to level one.  I made sure I had everything and headed up the
stairs.

On the Plane of Earth, my confused gold detection told me that the
portal was very close by.  I used the minotaur's wand of digging just
three times and I was there.  Air was a little harder.  I kept getting
engulfed by the elementals, and only twice by vortices.  Finally I got
to the portal to Fire.  Fire was probably the most difficult of the
elemental planes.  I used my confused gold detection to find all the
fire traps, then put on my ring of levitation and started running.
Unfortunately, an Archon showed up and blinded me, then summoned
monsters all around me.  I wiped out most of them, then tried to give
the Archon the finger of death.  Oops, bad idea.  He yells "Thou shalt
pay for thine insolence!" and summons even MORE monsters.  Finger of
death made me a path through the mob, and I ran for the portal.  The
Water Plane was very easy because I had genocided ;.  I used confused
gold detection so I would be able to see the portal, then just wandered
around inside my bubble waiting for it to get close enough.  I beat up
some elementals with Frost Brand while I was waiting, then I headed
through to the Astral Plane.

Two-word description of the Astral Plane: extremely difficult.  I saw
Pestilence over to the right, so I headed that way.  I unlocked the
door, and out came some Angels of Moloch.  They were probably the most
difficult things to kill there, since they couldn't be killed by
finger/wand of death.  The priests' summon insects spell wasn't much of
a problem, except for the time it summoned a fire ant.  Pestilence was
almost as much of a problem as the angels, since apparently the Riders
resurrect themselves like trolls do.  I ended up killing Pestilence a
total of five times.  Once I actually got to the altar on the right, it
turned out to be the wrong one, so I had to fight my way back out of
the room.  I closed and locked the door (just in case) and headed over
toward the middle.  I was about to check where Death and Famine were
when I noticed that the door to the middle room was already open and
more obnoxious Angels of Moloch were coming out.  I figured I might as
well try my ring of conflict now that my worthless guardian angel was
gone.  Apparently it worked, because I started hearing noises from
inside the room.  I decided not to waste any time, and as soon as the
angel was dead, I fired a death ray into the room to clear a path to
the door.  I made it all the way to the altar and.... it was chaotic!!


So, thats the story of my first ever ascension.  I definitely forgot
about the order of a lot of stuff.  I know at some point I decided to
try pudding farming with a brown pudding at the altar on level 24,
which wasn't very effective since I was already crowned, which gave me
a high prayer timeout.  I also remember invoking the Eye to take me to
Sokoban, where I reverse-genocided nurses, I just have no idea when I
did so.

If you have any comments, questions, or advice for my next ascension,
please post them here!

 - Stuart


